  "guide": "Prepare with explicitly selected baseline and candidate source snapshots and separate test_*.py regression files; do not send secrets. Snapshots accept UTF-8 source files, not host paths, symlinks or submodules. The app runs pytest in the container without downloading dependencies. Include existing tests in the candidate. run starts a job; poll get with new request IDs and cancel if necessary. A supplied_case_verified report means the regression assertion failed on the baseline and passed on the candidate, and existing candidate tests passed. It does not prove the whole patch correct or secure. Test code is arbitrary code and could forge its reports; input hashes are provenance, not attestations. Dependencies are limited to the image; use a reviewed derived image for additional packages. Record report IDs in work, failure-to-regression and knowledge apps through the calling agent. Startup marks interrupted runs; they can be retried. Start the Rhyven service daemon before use.",
